Ban Mishu Allos is an assistant professor of medicine in the Division of
Infectious Diseases, Department of Medicine and the Department of
Preventive Medicine at Vanderbilt University School of Medicine in
Nashville, Tennessee. Her clinical work relates to HIV and other infectious
diseases; her research has focused on foodborne illness in general and
Campylobacter jejuni as a cause of Guillain-Barré syndrome in particular.

