 (sub c) St. Louis encephalitis
 (sub d) Eastern equine encephalitis

In the absence of an existing program, arbovirus surveillance should be
initiated as part of the disaster response plan. At the very least, these
programs should determine population indexes of key vector species, virus
infection rates in those species, and seroprevalence in sentinel or wild
animals. Additional useful information includes prevailing weather
conditions, time of year, human exposure, human population at risk,
historical patterns of arboviral disease, and the potential for imported
diseases (3).

(sub 1)Additional information may be obtained at
http://www.cdc.gov/ncidod/dvbid/arbor/arboinfo.htm

